※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=26 diag=none

※ '«' and '»' move the bits of a number the way the marks point.  What falls
※ off the end is gone: that is what a shift is, and it is why this does not
※ fault on bits lost the way an addition faults on a sum that does not fit.

let thirteen: u8 = 13u8
let one: u8 = 1u8

@[visible]
let halved: mut u8 = 0u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    halved ← thirteen » one
    thirteen « one
